      "amount": "1/2 tsp",
      "notes": "or to taste"
    },
    {
      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1/4 tsp",
      "notes": "or to taste"
    },
    {
      "name": "chicken broth",
      "amount": "1 cup",
      "notes": "low-sodium"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Heat a large skillet over medium-high heat",
    "Add the chopped onion and cook until translucent",
    "Add the diced potatoes and cook until they start to brown",
    "Add the katsuramuki-cut serrano ham and cook until lightly browned",
    "Add the sauerkraut, caraway seeds, paprika, salt, and pepper, and stir to combine",
    "Pour in the chicken broth and bring to a boil",
    "Reduce the heat to medium-low and simmer for 20 minutes",
    "Serve hot, garnished with chopped fresh parsley if desired",
    "Ensure poultry is cooked to an internal temperature of 74°C / 165°F (juices run clear, no pink remaining) before serving."
  ],
